From 7e82a819a9e5c00c169d210e2e1a1ce86fb57787 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Massimiliano Gubinelli <m.gubinelli@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 21:56:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] files: restore the cursor by following the saved path
 top-down

The saved path was only checked for its shape: after a file was changed
outside TeXmacs it could lead into material that is not accessible, for
instance the variable name of a with, where the next keystroke silently
edits the markup ("font-series" became "foZnt-series").

cursor-memory-target now follows the saved path from the root as long
as it goes through accessible children (tree-accessible-child?), clamps
string offsets, and where the path stops goes to the start of the
nearest accessible child (path-start). It replaces cursor-memory-valid?
and cursor-memory-subtree; the regression tests are updated accordingly.
